<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35212" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Permessus</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περμησσός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river in Bœotia sacred
				to Apollo and the Muses</i>, <i>which rises in
				Mount Helicon and flows into the Copaic lake</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 6,
				64</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Permessis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis or ĭdos, <i>adj. f.</i>, <i>Permessian</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 1,
				77, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 70,
				3</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Permessĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Permessian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Laud. Seren. 8</span></i>
			.</div>
